/-!
# The Igusa scheme and its integrality

The modular function field is the intermediate field of the Laurent-series
field generated by the `j`-function and its dilates at divisors of the
level.  Localizing the rational subring of denominators prime to a prime
`ℓ` at the two charts where `j` and `j⁻¹` are integral gives two affine
charts; their pushout gluing along the common localization is the Igusa
scheme.  Both charts are domains with a common dense open, and all stalks
are reduced, so the glued scheme is integral.
-/

@[expose] public section

noncomputable section

